      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the new class mean, we need to determine the total scores for the students on both the initial test and the subsequent test, then sum these total scores and divide by the total number of students. The class mean is found by calculating the average of these total scores.\n\n1. **Find the total score for the test of the first 30 students:** We know the mean score for the first 30 students is 72%. The total score of the 30 students is:\n   \\[\n   72\\%\\ \\text{score} \\times 30\\ \\text{students} = 7.2\\ \\text{points/student} \\times 30\\ \\text{students} = 216\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the total score for the test of the next 6 students:** We know the mean score for the next 6 students is 78%. The total score of the 6 students is:\n   \\[\n   78\\%\\ \\text{score} \\times 6\\ \\text{students} = 7.8\\ \\text{points/student} \\times 6\\ \\text{students} = 46.8\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum the total scores of both tests:** The total score for the entire class is the sum of the scores from both tests:\n   \\[\n   216 + 46.8 = 262.8\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the new class mean using the total scores and the total number of students:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{New class mean} = \\frac{\\text{Total score for the entire class}}{\\text{Total number of students}} = \\frac{262.8}{36}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Perform the division to find the new class mean:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{262.8}{36} = 7.2999\\ \\ldots = 7.3\\%\n   \\]\n\n6. **Conclusion:** The new class mean is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{7.3\\%}\n   \\]",
